# Git push credentials (template)
#
# Why this exists: VS Code signs in to GitHub through its own GitHub
# Authentication extension and hands git an in-memory askpass helper. Nothing is
# written to git's config or to a credential store on disk, so a plain terminal
# (or an agent shell) has no credentials at all and `git push` fails with
#   fatal: could not read Username for 'https://github.com'
#
# Copy this file to `.git-credentials.env` (already gitignored) and fill it in.
# Use a fine-grained Personal Access Token with "Contents: read and write" on
# this repository only -- NOT your account password.
#   https://github.com/settings/tokens
#
# Then push with:  ./scripts/git-push.sh [branch]
#
# Rotate or revoke the token from that same settings page if it ever leaks.

GITHUB_USERNAME=your-github-username
GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_replace_me
